		{
			dependencies: ["024BBC15CA0EA6E1"]
			description: [
				"Changing the temperature to reach ideal levels is one option, but it's not always possible. Instead, it's possible to insulate oneself from the harsh environment altogether. While certain armors have inherent insulation, this world holds more dangers than just the climate, and a fur coat, while fashionable, won't defend you from an angry mob of skeletons."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Luckily, the &6Sewing Table&r can solve that issue. By combining any armor piece with a piece of insulating material, that armor will receive some insulation points. Each piece of armor can be fitted with different amount of insulators, which will increase their respective insulation type."
				"-Helmets can have up to 4 insulators"
				"-Chestplates can have up to 6 insulators"
				"-Leggings can have up to 5 insulators"
				"-Boots can have up to 4 insulators"
			]
			id: "7B628288068C173C"
			subtitle: "Never give up the drip"
			tasks: [{
				id: "22A3F96DEA90DDB6"
				item: "cold_sweat:sewing_table"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Outfit repeater"
			x: 1.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["024BBC15CA0EA6E1"]
			description: [
				"Chameleons are funny little critters that live in tropical and arid regions of the world. They can be tamed by throwing spider eyes or raw fish at them, and can be used to locate hot, cold or humid biomes by feeding them certain items, listed in the next page. They also occasionally shed their skin and can be perched on your head."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"-To locate hot biomes, the chameleon must be fed dead bush, nether wart or cactus"
				"-To locate cold biomes, the chameleon must be fed snowball, beetroot or sweet berries"
				"-To locate humid biomes, the chameleon must be fed slimeball, ink sac or cocoa beans."
			]
			hide_dependent_lines: true
			icon: "cold_sweat:thermolith"
			id: "07060D1344DA19A4"
